  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 308 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nOverall Thursday will be very similar to today weather wise. The\nridge of high pressure will remain in place and highs in the \nmiddle 90s to around 100 will occur with heat index values \naround 100 to near 110. Gusty southwesterly winds will develop \nagain during the morning and afternoon hours, mainly west of \nHighway 65. There is a low chance for an isolated thunderstorm \nacross portions of central Missouri again Thursday \nafternoon/early evening. Coverage will again be limited with \nmost locations likely remaining dry. If a storm can develop, \nthere is the potential for a strong storm with gusty winds the \nmain risk. There is a Marginal (1 out of 5) Severe Thunderstorm\nRisk for potential for central MO on Thursday. \n\nThe upper level ridge of high pressure remains in place across\nthe area into this weekend. The hot conditions will continue\nwith highs in the middle 90s to around 100 degree, with lows\nonly cooling into the middle 70s to the lower 80s each day. The\narea will remain mainly dry Friday into the weekend. \n\nThe ensemble model members are showing the ridge shifting back\nto the west some early next week, with the upper level jet \nshifting a little further south. This will bring shower and \nthunderstorm chances (10-30%) back to portions of the area early\nnext week. There is still question on just how far south and \nwest this will occur as the upper level ridge may just push \nslightly back to the west.",
